---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';

import Site from '@/layouts/Site.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '@/components/ui/Breadcrumb.astro';
import Button from '@/components/ui/Button.astro';
import JsonLd from '@/components/ui/JsonLd.astro';
import Icon from '@/components/marketing/Icon.astro';

import riverValleyAerial from '@/assets/images/river-valley-aerial.jpg';
---

<Site
  title="The Property - Carinya Parc"
  description="Explore our 42-hectare property in The Branch, NSW - home to native woodland, river frontage, and the beginning of our ecological restoration journey."
  path="/about/the-property"
  image="/images/farm-track-gate.jpg"
>
  <JsonLd />

  <div class="isolate min-h-screen bg-paperbark">
    {/* Breadcrumb navigation */}
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[1240px] px-6 pt-8 lg:px-14">
      <Breadcrumb />
    </div>

    <div class="relative isolate overflow-hidden py-16 sm:py-24">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-[1240px] lg:flex lg:justify-between lg:px-14 xl:justify-end">
        <div class="lg:flex lg:w-1/2 lg:shrink lg:grow-0 xl:absolute xl:inset-y-0 xl:right-1/2 xl:w-1/2">
          <div class="relative h-80 lg:-ml-8 lg:h-auto lg:w-full lg:grow xl:ml-0">
            <Image
              src={riverValleyAerial}
              alt="Aerial view of Carinya Parc property"
              widths={[640, 1080, 1600]}
              sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 50vw"
              quality={80}
              loading="eager"
              fetchpriority="high"
              class="absolute inset-0 size-full bg-line/40 object-cover"
            />
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="px-6 lg:contents">
          <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl pt-16 pb-24 sm:pt-20 sm:pb-32 lg:mr-0 lg:ml-8 lg:w-full lg:max-w-lg lg:flex-none lg:pt-32 xl:w-1/2">
            <p class="text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.24em] text-bracken-500">
              Our Land
            </p>
            <h1 class="mt-3.5 font-heading text-4xl font-normal tracking-tight text-pretty text-eucalypt-600 sm:text-5xl">
              The Property
            </h1>
            <p class="mt-6 text-xl/8 text-charcoal">
              Carinya Parc is 42 hectares (approximately 102 acres) of gently undulating countryside
              at The Branch, on New South Wales's mid-north coast.
            </p>
            <div class="mt-10 max-w-xl text-base/7 text-charcoal lg:max-w-none">
              <p>
                The site runs for more than 400 metres along the Branch River, offering natural
                frontage that supports swimming holes, fishing and, in time, improved riparian
                habitat. Scattered remnants of native woodland peek through cleared paddocks,
                hinting at the bush corridors we are reestablishing to connect fragmented habitats
                for koalas, gliders and native birds. A network of five farm dams, gravity-fed
                irrigation lines and four troughs ensures reliable water supply across the property,
                while a sealed driveway and visitor parking beside the homestead provide easy access
                for guests and volunteers.
              </p>
              <ul role="list" class="mt-8 space-y-8 text-charcoal">
                <li class="flex gap-x-3">
                  <Icon name="map-pin" class="mt-1 size-5 flex-none text-eucalypt-600" />
                  <span>
                    Located in NSW's mid-north coast, 5 km from Stroud, 70 km to Newcastle, and
                    within easy reach of Barrington Tops National Park, Port Stephens, and the Great
                    Lakes region.
                  </span>
                </li>
                <li class="flex gap-x-3">
                  <Icon name="clock" class="mt-1 size-5 flex-none text-eucalypt-600" />
                  <span>
                    Previously an alpaca farm, Carinya Parc has entered a deliberate rest period in
                    early 2024 to allow natural regeneration following decades of grazing pressure.
                  </span>
                </li>
                <li class="flex gap-x-3">
                  <Icon name="droplets" class="mt-1 size-5 flex-none text-eucalypt-600" />
                  <span>
                    The property includes five farm dams across undulating hills, frost-free ridges
                    and sheltered valleys. The Branch River frontage provides important riparian
                    habitat for local wildlife.
                  </span>
                </li>
              </ul>
              <h2 class="mt-16 font-heading text-2xl font-normal tracking-tight text-eucalypt-600">
                A Canvas for Ecological Renewal
              </h2>
              <p class="mt-6">
                Carinya Parc is a blank canvas poised for ecological renewal. Over the coming years
                we will plant more than 30,000 native trees and shrubs across five carefully defined
                zones, stabilise eroded riverbanks, trial syntropic agroforestry guilds and monitor
                soil health, water quality and biodiversity through an open-data framework. Every
                contour, watercourse and forest remnant has been mapped to guide this long-term
                vision, ensuring that each hectare moves steadily closer to its natural potential.
              </p>
              <p class="mt-6">
                Whether you are here to learn, to lend a hand or simply to enjoy the peace and
                privacy of rural NSW, The Property at Carinya Parc offers both a working farm and a
                living laboratory for regeneration in action.
              </p>
              <div class="mt-10 flex items-center gap-x-6">
                <Button href="/regenerate/" variant="bracken">
                  Get Involved
                </Button>
                <a
                  href="/about/"
                  class="text-sm font-semibold leading-6 text-eucalypt-600 hover:opacity-70"
                >
                  <span>
                    Learn more about us <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
                  </span>
                </a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Site>
